       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That's double the maximum daily dose for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day for prescription use. A single dose of 1600 mg is also above the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose. At this dose the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nHere are some options within the labeled limits:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), which is the maximum.\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **400 to 800 mg PO three times daily** (1,200 to 2,400 mg/day).\n\nIf you meant a different dose, such as 800 mg or 1600 mg total per day, tell me and I'll enter it. If the patient needs more analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect than the maximum dose gives, you could add a multimodal option like scheduled acetaminophen. That decision is yours or pharmacy's to make."
      }
